<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>Dependency-free cryptographic primitives for the SharedKernel: secret-agnostic one-way hashing (PBKDF2-HMACSHA256, suitable for passwords, API keys, recovery codes, and other one-way secrets), AES-256-GCM symmetric encryption (sync and async, plus an additive envelope-encryption seam and a bounded-TTL caching decorator for the key provider), RSA/ECDSA asymmetric signing, HMACSHA256 signing, and cryptographically secure random/token generation. Pure BCL System.Security.Cryptography only — zero third-party NuGet dependencies. AOT-compatible. Decoupled from identity/OIDC concerns so non-web worker services can consume it directly. Depends on SharedKernel.Primitives and SharedKernel.Configuration. v2.0.0: IPasswordHasher renamed to IOneWayHasher (breaking) to remove auth-domain vocabulary from a 01.Core primitive. Shipped (P-446/WO-068): IEncryptionKeyProvider's GetCurrentKey()/GetKey(string) synchronous members were removed and replaced by GetCurrentKeyAsync/GetKeyAsync; ISymmetricEncryptionService gained additive EncryptAsync/DecryptAsync/EncryptToStringAsync/DecryptToStringAsync overloads. Next breaking release (P-491/WO-081): every ISymmetricEncryptionService member (Encrypt/EncryptAsync/Decrypt/DecryptAsync/EncryptToString(Async)/DecryptToString(Async)) gains a required byte[] associatedData parameter with no default value — every call site across every consuming domain must add an explicit argument (pass Array.Empty&lt;byte&gt;() when no natural context binding exists); a mismatched associatedData at decrypt time fails authentication exactly like a tampered ciphertext or wrong key (see README's "Symmetric Encryption" section for the full migration table and an AAD usage example).</Description>
    <PackageTags>shared-kernel;cryptography;one-way-hashing;password-hashing;aes-gcm;encryption;envelope-encryption;signing;rsa;ecdsa;hmac;secure-random;aot</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SharedKernel.Primitives\SharedKernel.Primitives.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SharedKernel.Configuration\SharedKernel.Configuration.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
